WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.532
Do you know what animal is the tallest in the world?

2
00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:07.342
You guessed it! It's the giraffe!

3
00:00:07.343 --> 00:00:14.799
Follow me and let's take a close-up look at these marvelous creatures.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.700
Here we see a group of giraffes.

5
00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:22.459
As you can see, giraffes are the tallest animals in the world.

6
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.565
The male giraffe can grow to 5.5 meters.

7
00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:31.140
The female giraffe is usually a little bit shorter.

8
00:00:31.141 --> 00:00:34.500
What makes these animals so unusual?

9
00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:39.062
It's their very, very, very long necks, of course.

10
00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:44.602
Actually, this neck makes it possible for the giraffe to reach very high.

11
00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:49.071
It can reach the soft and tender leaves on the tops of trees.

12
00:00:49.072 --> 00:00:52.888
As you can see, there aren't many trees around here.

13
00:00:52.889 --> 00:00:59.295
So the giraffe's long neck helps it find food to stay alive.

14
00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:02.269
Can you see that giraffe over there?

15
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:06.628
Look at how the giraffe must spread its legs very wide.

16
00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:10.500
It's the only way it can get its head down low.

17
00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.130
Why is that?

18
00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:17.679
The giraffe's neck is very long, but it is not very flexible.

19
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.869
In fact, the giraffe's neck has only seven vertebrae.

20
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.005
We humans have seven vertebrae too.

21
00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:27.843
But look how short our necks are!

22
00:01:27.844 --> 00:01:34.049
With such big bones, the giraffe's neck cannot bend very well.

23
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:39.182
The giraffe's neck is not the only unusual thing about this animal!

24
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:45.207
The giraffe has a tongue that can stretch to almost 45 centimeters long.

25
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:49.738
Also, its head can stretch almost in a straight line.

26
00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:53.327
So, the giraffe can reach the highest leaves.

27
00:01:53.328 --> 00:01:58.874
In fact, a giraffe eats about 34 kilograms of leaves a day!

28
00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:04.577
The giraffe doesn't drink often─maybe once every two or three days.

29
00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:09.606
It gets water from the soft leaves!

30
00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:13.409
You know, the giraffe's body is not very big.

31
00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:18.611
In fact, the giraffe's body is about the size of a horse's body.

32
00:02:18.612 --> 00:02:24.940
But it's the legs and the neck that make it the tallest animal in the world!

33
00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:28.299
The legs of a giraffe are very strong!

34
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.420
The body of a giraffe is designed to support the head.

35
00:02:32.421 --> 00:02:36.110
See the large muscles at the top of its legs?

36
00:02:36.111 --> 00:02:38.764
Those muscles are powerful.

37
00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:44.935
A lion that attacks a giraffe will quickly learn that from a kick!

38
00:02:44.936 --> 00:02:51.060
Even though the giraffe has such a long neck, its voice box is very small.

39
00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:54.432
Giraffes aren't able to make loud noises.

40
00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:59.860
We usually don't hear them making any noises at all.

41
00:02:59.861 --> 00:03:02.872
Then how do they protect themselves?

42
00:03:02.873 --> 00:03:05.801
Well, you know how they can kick!

43
00:03:05.802 --> 00:03:09.607
Also, the giraffe's ears are very sensitive.

44
00:03:09.608 --> 00:03:13.678
So is its nose.

45
00:03:13.679 --> 00:03:21.657
In fact, a giraffe will often smell danger and use its very long legs to run away quickly!

46
00:03:21.658 --> 00:03:24.514
Its best protection is its color.

47
00:03:24.515 --> 00:03:29.628
It's hard to see a giraffe because it looks like it's a part of a tree.

48
00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:33.576
Giraffes don't sleep more than thirty minutes a day.

49
00:03:33.577 --> 00:03:43.987
Sometimes you'll see a giraffe lying down for a short time to rest, but many times they rest with their eyes open!

50
00:03:43.988 --> 00:03:48.361
Well, I hope you enjoyed your close-up view of the giraffe.

51
00:03:48.362 --> 00:03:50.054
Aren't they amazing?

52
00:03:50.055 --> 00:03:53.682
The next time you see a giraffe, remember:

53
00:03:53.683 --> 00:04:00.246
there's much more to this unusual animal than just its long neck!

